  "limitations": "The rook-graph formula is an exact reduction to the classical Zarankiewicz number, not a general closed form. The ordinary mutual-visibility forbidden-subgraph correspondences and the Turan, saturation, Bollobas-Wessel, and projective-plane ingredients are prior work. Connected mutual visibility is very recent, leaving residual risk from unindexed parallel work or later revisions. Finite verification supports but does not replace the symbolic proof. No independent validation is asserted.",
